By adding a series of discrete vortex rings located in the neighbourhood of the rotor, inflow fluctuations are modeled as the inflow value depends on the actual position of these rings. When this is added to a baseline dynamic inflow model, a better match with experimental data is obtained both in axial flight and in inclined de
